Serialize a result with invalid UTF-8 replaced instead of throwing.

A generated token can hold a byte that is not valid UTF-8 on its own, such as the byte-fallback
token 0xA2. The server's UTF-8 check only holds back a character that is cut off at the end of
the generated text, so the byte reached action_get_result, and dump() threw
"invalid UTF-8 byte at index 0: 0xA2" (json.exception.type_error.316). The call then failed in
wllama_action, and the worker crashed with every request it was running.

The llama.cpp HTTP server serializes the same results with safe_json_to_str(), which writes
U+FFFD in place of each invalid byte. This does the same.

This is the get_result part of ngxson/wllama#376, applied to the pinned source.

diff --git a/cpp/wllama-context.h b/cpp/wllama-context.h
index 29f890b..0aa7ab9 100644
--- a/cpp/wllama-context.h
+++ b/cpp/wllama-context.h
@@ -922,7 +922,7 @@ struct wllama_context
 
     res.success.value = true;
     res.has_more.value = has_more;
-    res.data_json.value = result ? data_json.dump() : "";
+    res.data_json.value = result ? safe_json_to_str(data_json) : "";
     res.is_error.value = is_error;
 
     if (!has_more)
